Good morning,

We are instructed to notify hail and wind damage on behalf of our client Sundale Property Group, LLC at their Windrow Grove community. Our reference is KRP/HAB/2025/7735.

Policy number: CP-7735-19042
Insured name: Sundale Property Group, LLC
Date of loss: 19 April 2026
Loss location: 6120 East 91st Street, Tulsa, OK 74137
Cause: Hail and straight-line wind
Estimated loss: USD 2,400,000

A severe thunderstorm crossed south Tulsa on Sunday evening. Hail to 2.25
inches and gusts to 71 mph were recorded nearby. Six of the twelve residential
roofs are damaged, the clubhouse skylight is out, and nine carport bays are
crushed - one onto a resident's car.

Four upper-floor units in Building 05 took water when the wind removed decking.
Two of those have had ceilings come down and all four are uninhabitable. Our
client has moved two households into vacant units on site and two into a hotel.

I should flag that we expect a scope discussion on the cosmetic damage
exclusion. Our consultant has cut test squares and documented mat fracture
rather than granule loss, and his report addresses the distinction directly.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * roof consultant's report
  * reinstatement schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster. Our client would also like
your confirmation of how the per-building wind and hail deductible will be
applied across the seven affected buildings.

